message: If you use these materials, please cite them as below.
type: dataset
title: 'Project O.R.A.C.L.E. — A GenAI-Enhanced International Relations Lab'
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-19
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: https://github.com/DTC-Consortium/DTC-Consortium-MLU
url: https://github.com/DTC-Consortium/DTC-Consortium-MLU/tree/main/mlu/course-elements/mlu-000009-project-oracle-ir-lab
abstract: >-
  A 1-credit lab module that gives International Relations students the hands-on research
  laboratory their STEM peers already have. A fictional 2025 alien-contact scenario casts
  students as "non-expert but educated analysts" and scaffolds them from finding where AI
  fails in Lab 1 to building a PartyRock app that works around those limits in Lab 2. The
  target it is built against is fluent-but-shallow AI output, and it closes with a
  one-on-one oral defense where students justify their research design and their AI use in
  person.
authors:
